<section data-panel="moodle" hidden aria-labelledby="moodle-heading">
    <div class="page-heading">
        <div>
            <div class="eyebrow">CONNECTED CAMPUS</div>
            <h1 id="moodle-heading">Moodle integration<span class="brand-dot">.</span></h1>
            <p>An optional connection, controlled by your institution.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="row g-4">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-8">
            <section class="surface p-4" aria-labelledby="moodle-connection-heading">
                <h2 id="moodle-connection-heading">Connection status</h2>
                <p id="moodle-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading institutional status…</p>
                <p id="moodle-check-help">A connection check reads Moodle service metadata only. It does not request individual users, courses or grades.</p>
                <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                    <button type="button" id="moodle-check" class="btn btn-primary" disabled aria-describedby="moodle-check-help">
                        Check Moodle connection
                    </button>
                    <button type="button" id="moodle-refresh" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Refresh status</button>
                </div>
                <div id="moodle-results" class="mt-4" hidden></div>
            </section>
            <section class="surface p-4 mt-4" id="moodle-section-area" hidden aria-labelledby="moodle-section-heading">
                <h2 id="moodle-section-heading">Course sections &amp; access</h2>
                <p>Connect a published SIS section to its independently verified Moodle course. The background worker manages student and instructor access without deleting learning records.</p>
                <form id="moodle-section-search-form">
                    <label for="moodle-section-search" class="form-label">Search by section code</label>
                    <div class="d-flex gap-2">
                        <input id="moodle-section-search" class="form-control" type="search" minlength="2" maxlength="80" required autocomplete="off">
                        <button class="btn btn-outline-primary" type="submit">Find sections</button>
                    </div>
                </form>
                <p id="moodle-section-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="mt-3">Search to load up to 20 matching sections.</p>
                <div id="moodle-section-results"></div>
            </section>
            <section class="surface p-4 mt-4" aria-labelledby="moodle-installation-heading">
                <h2 id="moodle-installation-heading">Approved Moodle installation</h2>
                <p>Review the installation before creating identity or section links. This approval does not enable single sign-on or synchronization.</p>
                <p id="moodle-installation-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" tabindex="-1">Loading saved approval…</p>
                <div id="moodle-installation-saved" hidden></div>
                <form id="moodle-installation-form">
                    <label for="moodle-installation-reason" class="form-label">Reason for approving this installation</label>
                    <textarea id="moodle-installation-reason" class="form-control" rows="2" maxlength="500" required aria-describedby="moodle-installation-help" disabled></textarea>
                    <p id="moodle-installation-help" class="form-text">Use an administrative reason. Do not include student information or credentials. The optional etSIS Moodle connector must be installed and enabled.</p>
                    <button type="submit" id="moodle-installation-review" class="btn btn-outline-primary" disabled>Review installation</button>
                </form>
                <div id="moodle-installation-preview" class="mt-4" hidden></div>
                <div id="moodle-installation-approval" class="mt-3" hidden>
                    <div class="form-check mb-3">
                        <input type="checkbox" id="moodle-installation-acknowledge" class="form-check-input">
                        <label for="moodle-installation-acknowledge" class="form-check-label">I checked the fingerprint against the Moodle installation approved by my institution.</label>
                    </div>
                    <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                        <button type="button" id="moodle-installation-confirm" class="btn btn-primary" disabled>Approve reviewed installation</button>
                        <button type="button" id="moodle-installation-cancel" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Cancel review</button>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <button type="button" id="moodle-installation-verify" class="btn btn-outline-primary mt-3" hidden disabled>Verify approved installation</button>
            </section>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-4">
            <aside class="surface p-4" aria-labelledby="moodle-institution-heading">
                <h2 id="moodle-institution-heading">Your institution decides</h2>
                <p>Moodle is not required for normal SIS workflows. A deployment administrator enables and configures it using protected server settings.</p>
                <p>Credentials stay on the server. This screen cannot display or change them.</p>
                <h3 class="h5">Following stages</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Automatic student and faculty accounts</li>
                    <li>Create other Moodle accounts from person records</li>
                    <li>Section, instructor and registration synchronization</li>
                    <li>Institutional single sign-on</li>
                    <li>Reviewed gradebook synchronization</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="mb-0">These stages are not enabled by a successful connection check. Academic records remain unchanged.</p>
            </aside>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
